[3.044882, "o", "al uses the compact single-page projection while a 160x38 terminal remains in the ordinary wide sidebar-\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[6;44H  plus-agent layout. Cite the exact responsive-layout symbols and one existing focused test. Suggest one website-recorder assertion that\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[7;44H  prevents a desktop demo from accidentally using compact mode.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[8;44H\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;147m\n●\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1mVerify responsive layout gates\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\u001b[10;44H  \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;5;110mpresentation_for_geometry()\u001b[38;5;252m selects the projection from geometry with hysteresis.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[11;44H  From \u001b[38;5;110mWorkspacePresentation.WIDE\u001b[38;5;252m it enters \u001b[38;5;179mCOMPACT\u001b[38;5;252m when either dimension is cramped: width < COMPACT_ENTER_WIDTH (80) or height <\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[12;44H  COMPACT_ENTER_HEIGHT (24).\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[13;44H  76x30: width 76 < 80, so it returns \u001b[38;5;179mCOMPACT\u001b[38;5;252m even though 30 rows clear the height gate.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[14;44H  160x38: 160 ≥ 80 and 38 ≥ 24, so it stays \u001b[38;5;179mWIDE\u001b[38;5;252m with sidebar plus agent. COMPACT_EXIT_WIDTH/HEIGHT (84/26) only applies once already compact.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[15;44H  Existing focused test: \u001b[38;5;114mtests/test_agent_workspace.py::test_compact_presentation_uses_two_dimensional_hysteresis\u001b[38;5;252m pins both width and height\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[16;44H  behavior.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[17;44H  Recorder guard: pass each non-mobile profile through presentation_for_geometry and assert \u001b[38;5;110mWorkspacePresentation.WIDE\u001b[38;5;252m.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[18;44H\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u